{
	"_comment": "Expansion-delay vectors replayed by the Windows engine (tests/unit/modules/hotstrings/engine/test_time_gate_corpus.ahk) and the macOS delay gate (tests/unit/modules/keymap/test_time_gate_corpus.lua). Definition: the expansion delay is the time between the LAST LETTER OF THE INPUT and the EXPANDER, to decide whether to give the output. The expander is the magic key when the trigger ends with it (the last input letter is then the one just before it), and otherwise the end character that completes the trigger (Space, punctuation...; for the Space tap-hold, the press, not the release). So the reference character is always the character typed immediately before the expander, the reference time is its key-down tick and the end time is the expander's key-down tick. Times are milliseconds on one clock; the configured seconds are rounded to whole milliseconds and compared with the elapsed whole milliseconds; the gate fires when elapsed <= delay (the exact deadline instant fires, one millisecond later does not); a delay of 0 means no gate; a missing reference time fails closed.",
